(text "Default build: VOUT = 1.8 V (fixed resistors - no trimmer). Pin-compatible family: pin1 ADJ/SET, pin2 + tab OUT, pin3 IN.\nOther outputs: change only the programming resistor(s) per the VOUT table." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 19.30 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4d282920-c27e-4ec5-affe-d0931eb1c8a6"))
(text "DESIGN EQUATIONS - NCP1117 (onsemi NCP1117/D datasheet)\nDesign point: VOUT 1.8 V (default), VIN 5.0 V nominal (3.3 V rail also checked), IOUT rated 1.0 A, SOT-223\nOutput: VOUT = VREF*(1 + R2/R1) + IADJ*R2 ; VREF = 1.25 V, IADJ = 52 uA typ (120 max)\n  Min-load rule: VREF/R1 >= IMIN = 5 mA max -> R1 <= 250 ohm ; R1 = 124 ohm (divider current 10.1 mA)\n  R2 = (VOUT - VREF)/(VREF/R1 + IADJ) = 54.3 ohm -> 54.9 ohm (E96) ; VOUT = 1.8063 V (+0.35%)\n  IADJ error at IADJ max = 6.6 mV ; VREF tolerance +/-1% (25C) / +/-2% (full temp) dominates\n  R1 dissipation = VREF^2/R1 = 12.6 mW ; R2 = 5.6 mW (0603 OK)\nPSRR: ripple gain = VOUT/VREF = 1.44 -> PSRR degrades 3.2 dB without CADJ\n  CADJ > 1/(2*pi*f*R1): 120 Hz -> 10.7 uF ; 100 kHz post-regulator -> 12.8 nF\nDropout: VDO = 1.2 V max @ 0.8 A (over temp) -> VIN(min) = VOUT + VDO = 3.00 V at full load\n  3.3 V rail: headroom 1.50 V vs VDO 1.2 V -> OK ; 5 V rail: headroom 3.20 V -> OK\nCurrent limit: 1.0 A min / 1.5 A typ ; VIN(max) = 20 V\nCapacitors: COUT >= 4.7 uF with ESR 33 mohm (typ) to 2.2 ohm; ceramic, tantalum or Al allowed if inside the ESR window (Fig.12/13).\nTHERMAL (thetaJA = 160 C/W, SOT-223 minimum pad; ~70 C/W with 1 in2 Cu (Fig.21); TJ(max) 125 C)\n  VIN 5.0 V: efficiency = VOUT*IOUT/(VIN*(IOUT+Idiv)) = 36% (max VOUT/VIN = 36%) ; temp rise dT = thetaJA*PD = 512 C\n  VIN 5.0 V: PD = (VIN-VOUT)*IOUT = 3.20*1.0 = 3.20 W -> TJ = 537C @25C / 597C @85C ; thermal IOUT(max) = 0.15 A @TA50C, 0.08 A @TA85C\n  VIN 3.3 V: efficiency = VOUT*IOUT/(VIN*(IOUT+Idiv)) = 54% (max VOUT/VIN = 55%) ; temp rise dT = thetaJA*PD = 240 C\n  VIN 3.3 V: PD = (VIN-VOUT)*IOUT = 1.50*1.0 = 1.50 W -> TJ = 265C @25C / 325C @85C ; thermal IOUT(max) = 0.31 A @TA50C, 0.17 A @TA85C\n  PD(max) = (125 - TA)/thetaJA = 0.47 W @50C, 0.25 W @85C. Add copper / heatsink or pre-regulate to raise current." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 130.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "fee92ffc-5af3-414a-bdd5-f95d35116454"))
